<title>BELGIUM: Luxembourg's BIL to open Cayman Islands office.</title>
<headline>Luxembourg's BIL to open Cayman Islands office.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banque Internationale a Luxembourg (BIL) said in a statement on Monday it planned to open an office in the Cayman Islands by the end of April.</p>
<p>The new office is part of BIL international strategy in investment fund administration, in which the existing offices in Dublin and Singapore also will play a role.</p>
<p>BIL is owned by Belgian bank Credit Communal de Belgique (CCB)/Gemeentekrediet van Belgie (GKB), which has a cross-shareholdership alliance with French bank Credit Local de France (CLF).</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
